# Build settings for the MicroVM image, read by the Dockerfile's RUN steps (POSIX sh syntax).
#
# CreateMicrovmImage has no build-argument input, so `docker build --build-arg` has no
# equivalent there. deploy.sh writes a copy of this file into the build context with values
# from its environment (NODE_VERSION, UPDRAFT_SPEC, AGENT_PACKAGES, TOOL_PACKAGES,
# SYSTEM_PACKAGES, PYTHON_COMMAND, UV_VERSION, BROWSER_PACKAGES, PLAYWRIGHT_VERSION,
# PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS, REQUIRE_STATE_COMMANDS, ISOLATION_PACKAGES); edit the defaults here.

# Node.js release to install from nodejs.org (Updraft needs >= 22.13).
NODE_VERSION="24.22.3"

# npm spec of Updraft. Ignored when vendor/ contains an `npm pack` tarball (*.tgz).
UPDRAFT_SPEC="@allenheltondev/updraft@0.1.0"

# 1: the build fails when the installed Updraft has no `state merge` command (jobs could not
# save to the shared state database). Set 0 only together with SharedState=disabled.
REQUIRE_STATE_COMMANDS="1"

# What AgentIsolation=enforced needs (README, "Security model"): bubblewrap for the sandbox
# runtime that agents and verify commands run in, and nftables for the packet filter that
# keeps every user but root away from the execution role's credentials. Amazon Linux 2023
# names, not checked against the MicroVM base image. Empty only together with
# AgentIsolation=disabled: an enforced job refuses to start without them.
ISOLATION_PACKAGES="bubblewrap nftables"

# Agent CLIs to install with npm, space-separated. Claude Code by default. The review loop
# (`review` in the Updraft config) needs a reviewer that is a different agent from the one
# that wrote the code: "@anthropic-ai/claude-code @openai/codex" adds Codex, and its key goes
# into the agent-environment secret next to Claude's (README, "The review loop"). Kiro is not
# an npm package and cannot be listed here: see KIRO_INSTALL_COMMAND. Pin versions for
# repeatable builds.
AGENT_PACKAGES="@anthropic-ai/claude-code"

# Kiro CLI from Kiro’s signed Amazon Linux ARM64 RPM. Empty: no Kiro.
# The image checks kiro-cli both on PATH and inside the enforced job sandbox.
KIRO_INSTALL_COMMAND="sh /opt/updraft/install-kiro-rpm.sh"

# Toolchain the repositories need on PATH, installed globally with npm, space-separated.
# Both the agent and the action's verify commands see these. Runtimes and system packages
# belong in the Dockerfile; a project's own dependencies are installed per job (npm ci).
# A project that lists typescript in its devDependencies uses that version through npm
# scripts and npx; this global one is the fallback for a bare `tsc`.
TOOL_PACKAGES="typescript@7.0.2"

# System packages for the repositories, installed with the base image's package manager
# (dnf or microdnf), space-separated. The job runs as a non-root user and cannot install
# these itself. Defaults: Python with pip, a C/C++ toolchain and make (native npm modules
# and Python wheels compile with them), and small tools agents and test scripts reach for.
# The names are Amazon Linux 2023's and have not been checked against the MicroVM base
# image: the build installs them one at a time and, if any is unknown, fails at the end
# naming all of them, so one failed build tells you everything to fix here.
SYSTEM_PACKAGES="python3.12 python3.12-pip gcc gcc-c++ make jq unzip zip which procps-ng diffutils patch"

# The interpreter that `python` and `python3` should mean for the agent and the verify
# commands, linked into /usr/local/bin. Empty leaves the system's own python3 alone.
# /usr/bin/python3 is never replaced: the package manager depends on it.
PYTHON_COMMAND="python3.12"

# uv (the Python package and project manager), installed with pip for PYTHON_COMMAND.
# Empty skips it.
UV_VERSION="0.13.9"

# A headless browser for repositories with browser tests: Playwright and the browsers below,
# installed once into a shared directory (PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH=/opt/ms-playwright, set
# for every job). Empty PLAYWRIGHT_VERSION skips the download; the libraries still install.
#
# A project that pins its own Playwright needs the browser build of THAT version. When it
# differs from this one, `npx playwright install chromium` in the job (for example as the
# first verify command) downloads the matching build into the same directory; that needs no
# root, only the system libraries below, which is why they are in the image.
PLAYWRIGHT_VERSION="1.65.1"
PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS="chromium"

# Shared libraries and fonts a headless Chromium needs. `playwright install --with-deps`
# only knows apt, so they are listed here. Amazon Linux 2023 names, not checked against the
# MicroVM base image (see SYSTEM_PACKAGES); Playwright does not list Amazon Linux as a
# supported platform, so treat the browser as unverified until a test has run in it.
BROWSER_PACKAGES="nss atk at-spi2-atk cups-libs libdrm libxkbcommon libXcomposite libXdamage libXrandr libXfixes libxcb mesa-libgbm pango cairo alsa-lib dejavu-sans-fonts liberation-fonts"
